-- ccc4-s84-definitions.l4 -- section 84 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (PART III, Firearms and Other Weapons):
-- the definitions of subsection (1), the barrel-length rule of (2), the weapons deemed not to be firearms of (3) and (3.1),
-- the holder of (4), and the rules on subsequent offences of (5) and (6).  Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- Conventions (the brief's rule of 2026-10-29 and the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05):
--   * every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words (a "means" that is closed,
--     a flat negative, an "if" that fails); NOTHING ("not covered") otherwise.  Every JUST FALSE carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`; every NOTHING `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
--   * "prescribed" is "prescribed by the regulations" (s 84(1)), which are not among the sources: every "prescribed" fact is a MAYBE BOOLEAN input,
--     so that a caller who does not know the regulations says NOTHING and the answer is NOTHING, not FALSE.
--   * a term of section 2 is an input named `s 2 <term>: ...` of type MAYBE BOOLEAN; a term of this subsection that another definition uses
--     is an input named `s 84(1) <term>: ...` (the caller passes the answer of the function that defines it).
--   * Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision, so that no two parts can define the same name.

§ `Helpers: three-valued logic (these make no new answer: they carry JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING from the facts to the definition that quotes the text)`

-- Every condition of a limb must hold (the text joins the conditions with "and" or states them in one sentence).
-- JUST FALSE if one condition fails; else NOTHING if one condition is not covered; else JUST TRUE.
GIVEN conditions IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) conditions THEN JUST FALSE   -- propagates: a condition of the limb failed
        IF elem NOTHING conditions THEN NOTHING   -- propagates: a condition of the limb is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Some limb of a list that joins its limbs with "or" must hold.  JUST TRUE if one holds; else NOTHING if one is not covered; else JUST FALSE.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) some limb holds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST TRUE) limbs THEN JUST TRUE
        IF elem NOTHING limbs THEN NOTHING   -- propagates: no limb is certain and one is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- propagates: every limb failed

-- "not": JUST TRUE becomes JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE becomes JUST TRUE, NOTHING stays NOTHING (a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE).
GIVEN answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the answer reversed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF answer EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- propagates: the reverse of a yes
        IF answer EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- propagates: the reverse of "not covered" is "not covered"

§ `Section 84(1) -- Definitions (In this Part)`

-- src:1909 | ammunition means a cartridge containing a projectile designed to be discharged from a firearm and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, includes a caseless cartridge and a shot shell; (munitions)
@ref s 84(1) "ammunition" (src:1909)
DECLARE `s 84(1) ammunition kind` IS ONE OF
    `s 84(1) ammunition: a cartridge containing a projectile designed to be discharged from a firearm`
    `s 84(1) ammunition: a caseless cartridge`
    `s 84(1) ammunition: a shot shell`
    `s 84(1) ammunition: a thing that is none of those`

@ref s 84(1) "ammunition" (src:1909)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 84(1) ammunition kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) ammunition` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a cartridge containing a projectile designed to be discharged from a firearm` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a caseless cartridge` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a shot shell` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 84(1) ammunition: a thing that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "without restricting the generality of the foregoing"

-- src:1910 | antique firearm means
-- src:1911 | (a) any firearm manufactured before 1898 that was not designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition and that has not been redesigned to discharge such ammunition, or
-- src:1912 | (b) any firearm that is prescribed to be an antique firearm; (arme à feu historique)
@ref s 84(1) "antique firearm" (src:1910-1912)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the year in which it was manufactured` IS A NUMBER
      `it was designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been redesigned to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed to be an antique firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) antique firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any firearm that is prescribed to be an antique firearm"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "antique firearm means"
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `limb (a)`, `limb (b)`)
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, JUST (`the year in which it was manufactured` LESS THAN 1898), JUST (NOT `it was designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition`), JUST (NOT `it has been redesigned to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition`))
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, `it is prescribed to be an antique firearm`)

-- src:1913 | authorization means an authorization issued under the Firearms Act; (autorisation)
@ref s 84(1) "authorization" (src:1913)
GIVEN `it is an authorization issued under the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) authorization` MEANS
    IF `it is an authorization issued under the Firearms Act`
