    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "authorization means an authorization issued under the Firearms Act"

-- src:1914 | automatic firearm means a firearm that is capable of, or assembled or designed and manufactured with the capability of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger; (arme automatique)
@ref s 84(1) "automatic firearm" (src:1914)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is assembled or designed and manufactured with the capability of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) automatic firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "a firearm" (the answer of s 2 firearm is not covered)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "automatic firearm means a firearm that is capable of"
    WHERE
        `the conditions` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, JUST (`it is capable of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger` OR `it is assembled or designed and manufactured with the capability of discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger`))

