-- src:1918 | cross-bow means a device with a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock that is designed to propel an arrow, a bolt, a quarrel or any similar projectile on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person; (arbalète)
@ref s 84(1) "cross-bow" (src:1918)
GIVEN `it is a device with a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed to propel an arrow, a bolt, a quarrel or any similar projectile on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) cross-bow` MEANS
    IF     `it is a device with a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock`
       AND `it is designed to propel an arrow, a bolt, a quarrel or any similar projectile on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove`
       AND `it is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cross-bow means a device with a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock"

-- src:1919 | export means export from Canada and, for greater certainty, includes the exportation of goods from Canada that are imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada; (exporter)
