GIVEN `it is an export from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the exportation of goods from Canada that are imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) export` MEANS
    IF     `it is an export from Canada`
        OR `it is the exportation of goods from Canada that are imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "export means export from Canada"

-- src:1920 | firearm part means a barrel for a firearm, a slide for a handgun and any other prescribed part, but does not include, unless otherwise prescribed, a barrel for a firearm or a slide for a handgun if that barrel or slide is designed exclusively for use on a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm; (pièce d’arme à feu)
@ref s 84(1) "firearm part" (src:1920)
GIVEN `it is a barrel for a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a slide for a handgun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another part that is prescribed to be a firearm part` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the barrel or slide is designed exclusively for use on a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is otherwise prescribed that the barrel or slide is a firearm part` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) firearm part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the exclusion` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include, unless otherwise prescribed, a barrel for a firearm or a slide for a handgun"
        IF `the exclusion` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless otherwise prescribed"
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any other prescribed part"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "firearm part means a barrel for a firearm"
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `it is a barrel for a firearm`), (JUST `it is a slide for a handgun`), `it is another part that is prescribed to be a firearm part`)
        `the exclusion` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST (`it is a barrel for a firearm` OR `it is a slide for a handgun`)), (JUST `the barrel or slide is designed exclusively for use on a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm`), (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `it is otherwise prescribed that the barrel or slide is a firearm part`))

