-- src:1926 | non-restricted firearm means a firearm that is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm; (arme à feu sans restriction)
@ref s 84(1) "non-restricted firearm" (src:1926)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) restricted firearm: the firearm is a restricted firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) non-restricted firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a condition is the answer of another definition that is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "non-restricted firearm means a firearm that is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm"
    WHERE
        `the conditions` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm`), (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 84(1) restricted firearm: the firearm is a restricted firearm`))

