-- src:1929 | prohibited device means
-- src:1930 | (a) any component or part of a weapon, or any accessory for use with a weapon, that is prescribed to be a prohibited device,
-- src:1931 | (b) a handgun barrel that is equal to or less than 105 mm in length, but does not include any such handgun barrel that is prescribed, where the handgun barrel is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union,
-- src:1932 | (c) a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm,
-- src:1933 | (d) a cartridge magazine that is prescribed to be a prohibited device, or
-- src:1934 | (e) a replica firearm; (dispositif prohibé)
@ref s 84(1) "prohibited device" (src:1929-1934)
GIVEN `it is a component or part of a weapon, or an accessory for use with a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed to be a prohibited device` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a handgun barrel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the length of the handgun barrel in millimetres` IS A NUMBER
      `the handgun barrel is one that is prescribed (a barrel the definition does not include)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the handgun barrel is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) cartridge magazine: the thing is a cartridge magazine` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) replica firearm: the thing is a replica firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) prohibited device` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "that is prescribed to be a prohibited device"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibited device means"
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `limb (a)`, `limb (b)`, `limb (c)`, `limb (d)`, `limb (e)`)
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST `it is a component or part of a weapon, or an accessory for use with a weapon`), `it is prescribed to be a prohibited device`)
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST `it is a handgun barrel`), (JUST (`the length of the handgun barrel in millimetres` AT MOST 105)), (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` (`s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `the handgun barrel is one that is prescribed (a barrel the definition does not include)`, JUST `the handgun barrel is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union`))))
        `limb (c)` MEANS JUST `it is a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm`
        `limb (d)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 84(1) cartridge magazine: the thing is a cartridge magazine`, `it is prescribed to be a prohibited device`)
        `limb (e)` MEANS `s 84(1) replica firearm: the thing is a replica firearm`

-- src:1935 | prohibited firearm means
-- src:1936 | (a) a handgun that
-- src:1937 | (i) has a barrel equal to or less than 105 mm in length, or
-- src:1938 | (ii) is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge,
-- src:1939 | but does not include any such handgun that is prescribed, where the handgun is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union,
-- src:1940 | (b) a firearm that is adapted from a rifle or shotgun, whether by sawing, cutting or any other alteration, and that, as so adapted,
-- src:1941 | (i) is less than 660 mm in length, or
-- src:1942 | (ii) is 660 mm or greater in length and has a barrel less than 457 mm in length,
-- src:1943 | (c) an automatic firearm, whether or not it has been altered to discharge only one projectile with one pressure of the trigger,
-- src:1944 | (d) any firearm that is prescribed to be a prohibited firearm, or
-- src:1945 | (e) any unlawfully manufactured firearm regardless of the means or method of manufacture;
-- src:1946 | (e) a firearm that is not a handgun and that
-- src:1947 | (i) discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner,
-- src:1948 | (ii) was originally designed with a detachable cartridge magazine with a capacity of six cartridges or more, and
-- src:1949 | (iii) is designed and manufactured on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force; (arme à feu prohibée)
@ref s 84(1) "prohibited firearm" (src:1935-1949)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) handgun: the firearm is a handgun` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the length of its barrel in millimetres, measured as subsection 84(2) says` IS A NUMBER
      `it is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the handgun is one that is prescribed (a handgun the definition does not include)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the handgun is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is adapted from a rifle or shotgun, by sawing, cutting or any other alteration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its length in millimetres as so adapted` IS A NUMBER
      `s 84(1) automatic firearm: the firearm is an automatic firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed to be a prohibited firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is an unlawfully manufactured firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capacity in cartridges of the detachable cartridge magazine it was originally designed with (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER
      `it was designed and manufactured on or after the day on which the second paragraph (e) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) prohibited firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any firearm that is prescribed to be a prohibited firearm"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibited firearm means"
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `limb (a)`, `limb (b)`, `limb (c)`, `limb (d)`, `limb (e) (the first)`, `limb (e) (the second)`)
        -- (a) a handgun that (i) has a barrel equal to or less than 105 mm in length, or (ii) is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge, but does not include any such handgun that is prescribed, where the handgun is for use in international sporting competitions
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 84(1) handgun: the firearm is a handgun`, (`s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST (`the length of its barrel in millimetres, measured as subsection 84(2) says` AT MOST 105)), (JUST `it is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge`))), (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` (`s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `the handgun is one that is prescribed (a handgun the definition does not include)`, JUST `the handgun is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union`))))
        -- (b) a firearm that is adapted from a rifle or shotgun and that, as so adapted, (i) is less than 660 mm in length, or (ii) is 660 mm or greater in length and has a barrel less than 457 mm in length
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, (JUST `it is adapted from a rifle or shotgun, by sawing, cutting or any other alteration`), (JUST (`its length in millimetres as so adapted` LESS THAN 660 OR (`its length in millimetres as so adapted` AT LEAST 660 AND `the length of its barrel in millimetres, measured as subsection 84(2) says` LESS THAN 457))))
        -- (c) an automatic firearm, whether or not it has been altered to discharge only one projectile with one pressure of the trigger
        `limb (c)` MEANS `s 84(1) automatic firearm: the firearm is an automatic firearm`
        -- (d) any firearm that is prescribed to be a prohibited firearm
        `limb (d)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, `it is prescribed to be a prohibited firearm`)
        -- (e) (the first) any unlawfully manufactured firearm regardless of the means or method of manufacture
        `limb (e) (the first)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, JUST `it is an unlawfully manufactured firearm`)
        -- (e) (the second) a firearm that is not a handgun and that (i) discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner, (ii) was originally designed with a detachable cartridge magazine with a capacity of six cartridges or more, and (iii) is designed and manufactured on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force
        `limb (e) (the second)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 84(1) handgun: the firearm is a handgun`), (JUST `it discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner`), (JUST (`the capacity in cartridges of the detachable cartridge magazine it was originally designed with (0 if none)` AT LEAST 6)), (JUST `it was designed and manufactured on or after the day on which the second paragraph (e) comes into force`))

-- src:1950 | prohibited weapon means
-- src:1951 | (a) a knife that has a blade that opens automatically by gravity or centrifugal force or by hand pressure applied to a button, spring or other device in or attached to the handle of the knife, or
-- src:1952 | (b) any weapon, other than a firearm, that is prescribed to be a prohibited weapon; (arme prohibée)
@ref s 84(1) "prohibited weapon" (src:1950-1952)
GIVEN `it is a knife that has a blade that opens automatically by gravity or centrifugal force or by hand pressure applied to a button, spring or other device in or attached to the handle of the knife` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed to be a prohibited weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) prohibited weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "any weapon, other than a firearm, that is prescribed to be a prohibited weapon"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibited weapon means"
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST (JUST `it is a knife that has a blade that opens automatically by gravity or centrifugal force or by hand pressure applied to a button, spring or other device in or attached to the handle of the knife`), `limb (b)`)
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon`, (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`), `it is prescribed to be a prohibited weapon`)

-- src:1953 | prohibition order means an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament prohibiting a person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things; (ordonnance d’interdiction)
@ref s 84(1) "prohibition order" (src:1953)
GIVEN `it is an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it prohibits a person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) prohibition order` MEANS
    IF     `it is an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament`
       AND `it prohibits a person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibition order means an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament"

-- src:1954 | Registrar means the Registrar of Firearms appointed under section 82 of the Firearms Act; (directeur)
@ref s 84(1) "Registrar" (src:1954)
GIVEN `it is the Registrar of Firearms appointed under section 82 of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) Registrar` MEANS
    IF `it is the Registrar of Firearms appointed under section 82 of the Firearms Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Registrar means the Registrar of Firearms appointed under section 82 of the Firearms Act"

-- src:1955 | registration certificate means a registration certificate issued under the Firearms Act; (certificat d’enregistrement)
@ref s 84(1) "registration certificate" (src:1955)
GIVEN `it is a registration certificate issued under the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) registration certificate` MEANS
    IF `it is a registration certificate issued under the Firearms Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "registration certificate means a registration certificate issued under the Firearms Act"

-- src:1956 | replica firearm means any device that is designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, a firearm that is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile at a muzzle velocity exceeding 152.4 m per second and at a muzzle energy exceeding 5.7 Joules, and that itself is not a firearm, but does not include any such device that is designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, an antique firearm; (réplique)
@ref s 84(1) "replica firearm" (src:1956)
GIVEN `it is a device designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the muzzle velocity in metres per second at which the firearm it resembles is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` IS A NUMBER
      `the muzzle energy in joules at which the firearm it resembles is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2 firearm: the device itself is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) antique firearm: the firearm it resembles is an antique firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) replica firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the exclusion` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include any such device that is designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, an antique firearm"
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the exclusion` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 84(1) antique firearm is not covered
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "that itself is not a firearm" (the answer of s 2 firearm is not covered)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "replica firearm means any device that is designed or intended to exactly resemble"
    WHERE
        `the conditions` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST `it is a device designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, a firearm`), (JUST (`the muzzle velocity in metres per second at which the firearm it resembles is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` GREATER THAN 152.4)), (JUST (`the muzzle energy in joules at which the firearm it resembles is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` GREATER THAN 5.7)), (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 2 firearm: the device itself is a firearm`))
        `the exclusion` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST (JUST `it is a device designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, a firearm`), `s 84(1) antique firearm: the firearm it resembles is an antique firearm`)

-- src:1957 | restricted firearm means
-- src:1958 | (a) a handgun that is not a prohibited firearm,
-- src:1959 | (b) a firearm that
-- src:1960 | (i) is not a prohibited firearm,
-- src:1961 | (ii) has a barrel less than 470 mm in length, and
-- src:1962 | (iii) is capable of discharging centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner,
-- src:1963 | (c) a firearm that is designed or adapted to be fired when reduced to a length of less than 660 mm by folding, telescoping or otherwise, or
-- src:1964 | (d) a firearm of any other kind that is prescribed to be a restricted firearm; (arme à feu à autorisation restreinte)
@ref s 84(1) "restricted firearm" (src:1957-1964)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) handgun: the firearm is a handgun` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the length of its barrel in millimetres, measured as subsection 84(2) says` IS A NUMBER
      `it is capable of discharging centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shortest length in millimetres to which it is designed or adapted to be reduced by folding, telescoping or otherwise, to be fired (its length if it cannot be reduced)` IS A NUMBER
      `it is a firearm of another kind that is prescribed to be a restricted firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) restricted firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the limbs` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a firearm of any other kind that is prescribed to be a restricted firearm"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "restricted firearm means"
    WHERE
        `the limbs` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `limb (a)`, `limb (b)`, `limb (c)`, `limb (d)`)
        -- (a) a handgun that is not a prohibited firearm
        `limb (a)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 84(1) handgun: the firearm is a handgun`, (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm`))
        -- (b) a firearm that (i) is not a prohibited firearm, (ii) has a barrel less than 470 mm in length, and (iii) is capable of discharging centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner
        `limb (b)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm`), (JUST (`the length of its barrel in millimetres, measured as subsection 84(2) says` LESS THAN 470)), (JUST `it is capable of discharging centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner`))
        -- (c) a firearm that is designed or adapted to be fired when reduced to a length of less than 660 mm by folding, telescoping or otherwise
        `limb (c)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, JUST (`the shortest length in millimetres to which it is designed or adapted to be reduced by folding, telescoping or otherwise, to be fired (its length if it cannot be reduced)` LESS THAN 660))
        -- (d) a firearm of any other kind that is prescribed to be a restricted firearm
        `limb (d)` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`, `it is a firearm of another kind that is prescribed to be a restricted firearm`)

-- src:1965 | restricted weapon means any weapon, other than a firearm, that is prescribed to be a restricted weapon; (arme à autorisation restreinte)
@ref s 84(1) "restricted weapon" (src:1965)
GIVEN `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed to be a restricted weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) restricted weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the conditions` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "that is prescribed to be a restricted weapon"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "restricted weapon means any weapon, other than a firearm"
    WHERE
        `the conditions` MEANS `s 84(1) every condition of the limb holds` (LIST `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon`, (`s 84(1) the answer reversed` `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm`), `it is prescribed to be a restricted weapon`)

-- src:1966 | semi-automatic, in respect of a firearm, means that the firearm that is equipped with a mechanism that, following the discharge of a cartridge, automatically operates to complete any part of the reloading cycle necessary to prepare for the discharge of the next cartridge; (semi-automatique)
@ref s 84(1) "semi-automatic" (src:1966)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is equipped with a mechanism that, following the discharge of a cartridge, automatically operates to complete any part of the reloading cycle necessary to prepare for the discharge of the next cartridge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) semi-automatic` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a firearm"
        IF `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "in respect of a firearm" (the answer of s 2 firearm is not covered)
        IF `it is equipped with a mechanism that, following the discharge of a cartridge, automatically operates to complete any part of the reloading cycle necessary to prepare for the discharge of the next cartridge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "semi-automatic, in respect of a firearm, means"

-- src:1967 | superior court means
-- src:1968 | (a) in Ontario, the Superior Court of Justice, sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the relevant adjudication was made,
-- src:1969 | (b) in Quebec, the Superior Court,
-- src:1970 | (c) in New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta, the Court of Queen’s Bench, and
-- src:1971 | (d) in Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island, Newfoundland and Labrador and a territory, the Supreme Court; (cour supérieure)
-- src:1972 | (e) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 3]
@ref s 84(1) "superior court" (src:1967-1972)
DECLARE `s 84(1) superior court` IS ONE OF
    `s 84(1) superior court: the Superior Court of Justice, sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the relevant adjudication was made`
    `s 84(1) superior court: the Superior Court`
    `s 84(1) superior court: the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`

-- (a) Ontario; (b) Quebec; (c) New Brunswick, Manitoba, Saskatchewan and Alberta; (d) Nova Scotia, British Columbia, Prince Edward Island, Newfoundland and Labrador and a territory.
-- Finding: paragraph (d) says "a territory, the Supreme Court", and Nunavut is a territory, whereas s 2 "superior court of criminal jurisdiction" (f) names the Nunavut Court of Justice: encoded as this text has it (fork F-Nunavut).
@ref s 84(1) "superior court" (src:1967-1972)
GIVEN place IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A `s 84(1) superior court`
`s 84(1) the superior court in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN Ontario THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Superior Court of Justice, sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the relevant adjudication was made`
    WHEN Quebec THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Superior Court`
    WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Manitoba THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Saskatchewan THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN Alberta THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Court of Queen’s Bench`
    WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `British Columbia` THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`
    WHEN Yukon THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`
    WHEN Nunavut THEN `s 84(1) superior court: the Supreme Court`

@ref s 84(1) "superior court" (src:1967-1972)
GIVEN place IS A `Province or territory`
      court IS A `s 84(1) superior court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) superior court` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `s 84(1) the superior court in the place` place
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "superior court means"

-- (e) is shown repealed: "(e) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 3]".
-- src:1972 | (e) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 3]
@ref s 84(1) "superior court" (e), repealed (src:1972)
`s 84(1) superior court paragraph (e) as the text shows it` MEANS "(e) [Repealed, 2026, c. 11, s. 3]"

-- src:1973 | transfer means sell, provide, barter, give, lend, rent, send, transport, ship, distribute or deliver. (cession)
@ref s 84(1) "transfer" (src:1973)
DECLARE `s 84(1) transfer act` IS ONE OF
    `s 84(1) transfer: sell`
    `s 84(1) transfer: provide`
    `s 84(1) transfer: barter`
    `s 84(1) transfer: give`
    `s 84(1) transfer: lend`
    `s 84(1) transfer: rent`
    `s 84(1) transfer: send`
    `s 84(1) transfer: transport`
    `s 84(1) transfer: ship`
    `s 84(1) transfer: distribute`
    `s 84(1) transfer: deliver`
    `s 84(1) transfer: an act that is none of those`

@ref s 84(1) "transfer" (src:1973)
GIVEN act IS A `s 84(1) transfer act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) transfer` MEANS
    IF act EQUALS `s 84(1) transfer: an act that is none of those`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "transfer means sell, provide, barter, give, lend, rent, send, transport, ship, distribute or deliver"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 84(1) -- What the Part's definitions say about one thing: the seam the keel asks for (section 2.1), and the classes the offence sections name`

-- Section 2.1 says that fifteen terms, and authorization, licence and registration certificate used in relation to them, "have the same meaning as in subsection 84(1)".
-- The keel's function `s 2.1 the term has the meaning it has in subsection 84(1)` takes the answer of this part as an input: it is the function below.
-- The answers of the definitions above for ONE thing are gathered in a record; the function picks the one the term asks for.
-- src:1909 | ammunition means a cartridge containing a projectile designed to be discharged from a firearm and, without restricting the generality of the foregoing, includes a caseless cartridge and a shot shell; (munitions)
-- src:1910 | antique firearm means
-- src:1911 | (a) any firearm manufactured before 1898 that was not designed to discharge rim-fire or centre-fire ammunition and that has not been redesigned to discharge such ammunition, or
-- src:1912 | (b) any firearm that is prescribed to be an antique firearm; (arme à feu historique)
-- src:1913 | authorization means an authorization issued under the Firearms Act; (autorisation)
-- src:1914 | automatic firearm means a firearm that is capable of, or assembled or designed and manufactured with the capability of, discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger; (arme automatique)
-- src:1915 | cartridge magazine means a device or container from which ammunition may be fed into the firing chamber of a firearm; (chargeur)
-- src:1916 | chief firearms officer means a chief firearms officer as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act; (contrôleur des armes à feu)
-- src:1917 | Commissioner of Firearms means the Commissioner of Firearms appointed under section 81.1 of the Firearms Act; (commissaire aux armes à feu)
-- src:1918 | cross-bow means a device with a bow and a bowstring mounted on a stock that is designed to propel an arrow, a bolt, a quarrel or any similar projectile on a trajectory guided by a barrel or groove and that is capable of causing serious bodily injury or death to a person; (arbalète)
-- src:1919 | export means export from Canada and, for greater certainty, includes the exportation of goods from Canada that are imported into Canada and shipped in transit through Canada; (exporter)
-- src:1920 | firearm part means a barrel for a firearm, a slide for a handgun and any other prescribed part, but does not include, unless otherwise prescribed, a barrel for a firearm or a slide for a handgun if that barrel or slide is designed exclusively for use on a firearm that is deemed under subsection 84(3) not to be a firearm; (pièce d’arme à feu)
-- src:1921 | firearms officer means a firearms officer as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Firearms Act; (préposé aux armes à feu)
-- src:1922 | handgun means a firearm that is designed, altered or intended to be aimed and fired by the action of one hand, whether or not it has been redesigned or subsequently altered to be aimed and fired by the action of both hands; (arme de poing)
-- src:1923 | imitation firearm means any thing that imitates a firearm, and includes a replica firearm; (fausse arme à feu)
-- src:1924 | import means import into Canada and, for greater certainty, includes the importation of goods into Canada that are shipped in transit through Canada and exported from Canada; (importer)
-- src:1925 | licence means a licence issued under the Firearms Act; (permis)
-- src:1926 | non-restricted firearm means a firearm that is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm; (arme à feu sans restriction)
-- src:1927 | prescribed means prescribed by the regulations; (Version anglaise seulement)
-- src:1928 | prohibited ammunition means ammunition, or a projectile of any kind, that is prescribed to be prohibited ammunition; (munitions prohibées)
-- src:1929 | prohibited device means
-- src:1930 | (a) any component or part of a weapon, or any accessory for use with a weapon, that is prescribed to be a prohibited device,
-- src:1931 | (b) a handgun barrel that is equal to or less than 105 mm in length, but does not include any such handgun barrel that is prescribed, where the handgun barrel is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union,
-- src:1932 | (c) a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm,
-- src:1933 | (d) a cartridge magazine that is prescribed to be a prohibited device, or
-- src:1934 | (e) a replica firearm; (dispositif prohibé)
-- src:1935 | prohibited firearm means
-- src:1936 | (a) a handgun that
-- src:1937 | (i) has a barrel equal to or less than 105 mm in length, or
-- src:1938 | (ii) is designed or adapted to discharge a 25 or 32 calibre cartridge,
-- src:1939 | but does not include any such handgun that is prescribed, where the handgun is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union,
-- src:1940 | (b) a firearm that is adapted from a rifle or shotgun, whether by sawing, cutting or any other alteration, and that, as so adapted,
-- src:1941 | (i) is less than 660 mm in length, or
-- src:1942 | (ii) is 660 mm or greater in length and has a barrel less than 457 mm in length,
-- src:1943 | (c) an automatic firearm, whether or not it has been altered to discharge only one projectile with one pressure of the trigger,
-- src:1944 | (d) any firearm that is prescribed to be a prohibited firearm, or
-- src:1945 | (e) any unlawfully manufactured firearm regardless of the means or method of manufacture;
-- src:1946 | (e) a firearm that is not a handgun and that
-- src:1947 | (i) discharges centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner,
-- src:1948 | (ii) was originally designed with a detachable cartridge magazine with a capacity of six cartridges or more, and
-- src:1949 | (iii) is designed and manufactured on or after the day on which this paragraph comes into force; (arme à feu prohibée)
-- src:1950 | prohibited weapon means
-- src:1951 | (a) a knife that has a blade that opens automatically by gravity or centrifugal force or by hand pressure applied to a button, spring or other device in or attached to the handle of the knife, or
-- src:1952 | (b) any weapon, other than a firearm, that is prescribed to be a prohibited weapon; (arme prohibée)
-- src:1953 | prohibition order means an order made under this Act or any other Act of Parliament prohibiting a person from possessing any firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance, or all such things; (ordonnance d’interdiction)
-- src:1954 | Registrar means the Registrar of Firearms appointed under section 82 of the Firearms Act; (directeur)
-- src:1955 | registration certificate means a registration certificate issued under the Firearms Act; (certificat d’enregistrement)
-- src:1956 | replica firearm means any device that is designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, a firearm that is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile at a muzzle velocity exceeding 152.4 m per second and at a muzzle energy exceeding 5.7 Joules, and that itself is not a firearm, but does not include any such device that is designed or intended to exactly resemble, or to resemble with near precision, an antique firearm; (réplique)
-- src:1957 | restricted firearm means
-- src:1958 | (a) a handgun that is not a prohibited firearm,
-- src:1959 | (b) a firearm that
-- src:1960 | (i) is not a prohibited firearm,
-- src:1961 | (ii) has a barrel less than 470 mm in length, and
-- src:1962 | (iii) is capable of discharging centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner,
-- src:1963 | (c) a firearm that is designed or adapted to be fired when reduced to a length of less than 660 mm by folding, telescoping or otherwise, or
-- src:1964 | (d) a firearm of any other kind that is prescribed to be a restricted firearm; (arme à feu à autorisation restreinte)
-- src:1965 | restricted weapon means any weapon, other than a firearm, that is prescribed to be a restricted weapon; (arme à autorisation restreinte)
@ref s 84(1), the definitions that s 2.1 names (src:1909-1965)
DECLARE `s 84(1) the answers for the thing` HAS
    `the answer of s 84(1) ammunition`                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) antique firearm`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) automatic firearm`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) cartridge magazine`          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) cross-bow`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) firearm part`                IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) handgun`                     IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) imitation firearm`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited ammunition`       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited device`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited firearm`          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited weapon`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) replica firearm`             IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) restricted firearm`          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) restricted weapon`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) authorization`               IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) licence`                     IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the answer of s 84(1) registration certificate`    IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref s 84(1), the definitions that s 2.1 names (src:1909-1965)
GIVEN term IS A `s 2.1 term`
      answers IS A `s 84(1) the answers for the thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the thing is within the meaning the term has in subsection 84(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `ammunition` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) ammunition`
    WHEN `antique firearm` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) antique firearm`
    WHEN `automatic firearm` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) automatic firearm`
    WHEN `cartridge magazine` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) cartridge magazine`
    WHEN `cross-bow` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) cross-bow`
    WHEN `firearm part` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) firearm part`
    WHEN `handgun` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) handgun`
    WHEN `imitation firearm` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) imitation firearm`
    WHEN `prohibited ammunition` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited ammunition`
    WHEN `prohibited device` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited device`
    WHEN `prohibited firearm` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited firearm`
    WHEN `prohibited weapon` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) prohibited weapon`
    WHEN `replica firearm` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) replica firearm`
    WHEN `restricted firearm` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) restricted firearm`
    WHEN `restricted weapon` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) restricted weapon`
    WHEN `authorization, when used in relation to those words and expressions` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) authorization`
    WHEN `licence, when used in relation to those words and expressions` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) licence`
    WHEN `registration certificate, when used in relation to those words and expressions` THEN answers's `the answer of s 84(1) registration certificate`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 2.1 hands the meaning to subsection 84(1) only for the terms it names

-- Firearms come in three classes in subsection 84(1): the text defines "restricted firearm" as a firearm "that is not a prohibited firearm" and "non-restricted firearm" as a firearm that "is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm".
-- This function reads the three answers together, in that order, because the definitions are written to exclude one another.
-- src:1926 | non-restricted firearm means a firearm that is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm; (arme à feu sans restriction)
@ref s 84(1) "non-restricted firearm", the order of the three classes (src:1926)
DECLARE `s 84(1) class of firearm` IS ONE OF
    `s 84(1) class: a prohibited firearm`
    `s 84(1) class: a restricted firearm`
    `s 84(1) class: a non-restricted firearm`
    `s 84(1) class: not a firearm`
    `s 84(1) class: not covered`

@ref s 84(1) "non-restricted firearm", the order of the three classes (src:1926)
GIVEN `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) restricted firearm: the firearm is a restricted firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 84(1) class of firearm`
`s 84(1) the class of firearm it is` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `s 84(1) class: a prohibited firearm`
        IF `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `s 84(1) class: not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a prescription by the regulations decides whether it is a prohibited firearm
        IF `s 84(1) restricted firearm: the firearm is a restricted firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `s 84(1) class: a restricted firearm`
        IF `s 84(1) restricted firearm: the firearm is a restricted firearm` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `s 84(1) class: not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a prescription by the regulations decides whether it is a restricted firearm
        IF `s 84(1) non-restricted firearm` `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` `s 84(1) prohibited firearm: the firearm is a prohibited firearm` `s 84(1) restricted firearm: the firearm is a restricted firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN `s 84(1) class: a non-restricted firearm`
        IF `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN `s 84(1) class: not a firearm`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "non-restricted firearm means a firearm that is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm"
        OTHERWISE `s 84(1) class: not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 2 firearm is not covered

-- The things the offence sections of this Part name.  The classes are the terms of subsection 84(1) (and "weapon" and "explosive substance" of section 2 where an offence names them);
-- a thing is given the MOST SPECIFIC class that fits (prohibited ammunition is ammunition; a replica firearm is a prohibited device by paragraph (e) of that definition).
-- Each offence section tests the thing against the list that section writes out.
-- src:1929 | prohibited device means
-- src:1930 | (a) any component or part of a weapon, or any accessory for use with a weapon, that is prescribed to be a prohibited device,
-- src:1931 | (b) a handgun barrel that is equal to or less than 105 mm in length, but does not include any such handgun barrel that is prescribed, where the handgun barrel is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union,
-- src:1932 | (c) a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm,
-- src:1933 | (d) a cartridge magazine that is prescribed to be a prohibited device, or
-- src:1934 | (e) a replica firearm; (dispositif prohibé)
@ref s 84(1), the classes the offence sections name (src:1929-1934)
DECLARE `s 84(1) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm`
    `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`
    `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm`
    `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
    `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
    `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm`
    `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm`
    `s 84(1) kind: a firearm part`
    `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition`
    `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`
    `s 84(1) kind: a cross-bow`
    `s 84(1) kind: an explosive substance`
    `s 84(1) kind: a thing that is none of those`

-- Three groupings the offence sections use again and again.  They name the classes above that fall within a word the sections write as one word:
-- "a firearm" is a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm (the three classes the definitions exclude from one another);
-- "a prohibited device" includes a replica firearm (paragraph (e) of that definition);
-- "ammunition" is ammunition or prohibited ammunition (the definition of prohibited ammunition starts from ammunition).
-- src:1926 | non-restricted firearm means a firearm that is neither a prohibited firearm nor a restricted firearm; (arme à feu sans restriction)
@ref s 84(1) "non-restricted firearm", the three classes of firearm (src:1926)
GIVEN `the thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` MEANS
       `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm`
    OR `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`
    OR `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm`

-- src:1929 | prohibited device means
-- src:1930 | (a) any component or part of a weapon, or any accessory for use with a weapon, that is prescribed to be a prohibited device,
-- src:1931 | (b) a handgun barrel that is equal to or less than 105 mm in length, but does not include any such handgun barrel that is prescribed, where the handgun barrel is for use in international sporting competitions governed by the rules of the International Shooting Union,
-- src:1932 | (c) a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm,
-- src:1933 | (d) a cartridge magazine that is prescribed to be a prohibited device, or
-- src:1934 | (e) a replica firearm; (dispositif prohibé)
@ref s 84(1) "prohibited device", paragraph (e) a replica firearm (src:1929-1934)
GIVEN `the thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` MEANS
       `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm`
    OR `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm`

-- src:1928 | prohibited ammunition means ammunition, or a projectile of any kind, that is prescribed to be prohibited ammunition; (munitions prohibées)
@ref s 84(1) "prohibited ammunition" (src:1928)
GIVEN `the thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` MEANS
       `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: ammunition other than prohibited ammunition`
    OR `the thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`

§ `Section 84(2) -- Barrel length`

-- src:1974 | Barrel length
-- src:1975 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, the length of a barrel of a firearm is
-- src:1976 | (a) in the case of a revolver, the distance from the muzzle of the barrel to the breach end immediately in front of the cylinder, and
-- src:1977 | (b) in any other case, the distance from the muzzle of the barrel to and including the chamber,
-- src:1978 | but does not include the length of any component, part or accessory including any component, part or accessory designed or intended to suppress the muzzle flash or reduce recoil.
@ref s 84(2) (src:1974-1978)
GIVEN `it is a revolver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distance in millimetres from the muzzle of the barrel to the breach end immediately in front of the cylinder` IS A NUMBER
      `the distance in millimetres from the muzzle of the barrel to and including the chamber` IS A NUMBER
      `the length in millimetres of any component, part or accessory within that distance (including one designed or intended to suppress the muzzle flash or reduce recoil)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 84(2) the length of the barrel of a firearm in millimetres` MEANS
    IF `it is a revolver`
    THEN `the distance in millimetres from the muzzle of the barrel to the breach end immediately in front of the cylinder` MINUS `the length in millimetres of any component, part or accessory within that distance (including one designed or intended to suppress the muzzle flash or reduce recoil)`
    ELSE `the distance in millimetres from the muzzle of the barrel to and including the chamber` MINUS `the length in millimetres of any component, part or accessory within that distance (including one designed or intended to suppress the muzzle flash or reduce recoil)`

§ `Section 84(3) and (3.1) -- Certain weapons deemed not to be firearms`

-- src:1979 | Certain weapons deemed not to be firearms
-- src:1980 | (3) For the purposes of sections 91 to 95, 99 to 101, 103 to 107 and 117.03 of this Act and the provisions of the Firearms Act, the following weapons are deemed not to be firearms:
-- src:1981 | (a) any antique firearm;
-- src:1982 | (b) any device that is
-- src:1983 | (i) designed exclusively for signalling, for notifying of distress, for firing blank cartridges or for firing stud cartridges, explosive-driven rivets or other industrial projectiles, and
-- src:1984 | (ii) intended by the person in possession of it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed;
-- src:1985 | (c) any shooting device that is
-- src:1986 | (i) designed exclusively for the slaughtering of domestic animals, the tranquillizing of animals or the discharging of projectiles with lines attached to them, and
-- src:1987 | (ii) intended by the person in possession of it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed; and
-- src:1988 | (d) any other barrelled weapon, where it is proved that the weapon is not designed or adapted to discharge
-- src:1989 | (i) a shot, bullet or other projectile at a muzzle velocity exceeding 152.4 m per second or at a muzzle energy exceeding 5.7 Joules, or
-- src:1990 | (ii) a shot, bullet or other projectile that is designed or adapted to attain a velocity exceeding 152.4 m per second or an energy exceeding 5.7 Joules.
@ref s 84(3) (src:1979-1990)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the purpose is a provision of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 84(1) antique firearm: the weapon is an antique firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a device designed exclusively for signalling, for notifying of distress, for firing blank cartridges or for firing stud cartridges, explosive-driven rivets or other industrial projectiles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person in possession of it intends it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a shooting device designed exclusively for the slaughtering of domestic animals, the tranquillizing of animals or the discharging of projectiles with lines attached to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is any other barrelled weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the weapon is not designed or adapted to discharge such a projectile` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the muzzle velocity in metres per second at which it is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` IS A NUMBER
      `the muzzle energy in joules at which it is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` IS A NUMBER
      `the velocity in metres per second that a projectile it is designed or adapted to discharge is designed or adapted to attain` IS A NUMBER
      `the energy in joules that a projectile it is designed or adapted to discharge is designed or adapted to attain` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(3) the weapon is deemed not to be a firearm for the purposes of the provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the provision is one the subsection names`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 91 to 95, 99 to 101, 103 to 107 and 117.03 of this Act and the provisions of the Firearms Act"
        IF `s 84(1) antique firearm: the weapon is an antique firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)` OR `limb (d)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following weapons are deemed not to be firearms" (the list does not say "only")
    WHERE
        `the provision is one the subsection names` MEANS
               `the purpose is a provision of the Firearms Act`
            OR (provision's `section` AT LEAST 91 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 95)
            OR (provision's `section` AT LEAST 99 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 101)
            OR (provision's `section` AT LEAST 103 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 107)
            OR provision's `section` EQUALS 117.03
        -- (b) any device that is (i) designed exclusively for signalling, ... and (ii) intended by the person in possession of it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed
        `limb (b)` MEANS `it is a device designed exclusively for signalling, for notifying of distress, for firing blank cartridges or for firing stud cartridges, explosive-driven rivets or other industrial projectiles` AND `the person in possession of it intends it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed`
        -- (c) any shooting device that is (i) designed exclusively for the slaughtering of domestic animals, ... and (ii) intended ... exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed
        `limb (c)` MEANS `it is a shooting device designed exclusively for the slaughtering of domestic animals, the tranquillizing of animals or the discharging of projectiles with lines attached to them` AND `the person in possession of it intends it to be used exclusively for the purpose for which it is designed`
        -- (d) any other barrelled weapon, where it is proved that the weapon is not designed or adapted to discharge (i) a shot, bullet or other projectile at a muzzle velocity exceeding 152.4 m per second or at a muzzle energy exceeding 5.7 Joules, or (ii) a projectile designed or adapted to attain a velocity exceeding 152.4 m per second or an energy exceeding 5.7 Joules
        `limb (d)` MEANS
                `it is any other barrelled weapon`
            AND `it is proved that the weapon is not designed or adapted to discharge such a projectile`
            AND `the muzzle velocity in metres per second at which it is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` AT MOST 152.4
            AND `the muzzle energy in joules at which it is designed or adapted to discharge a shot, bullet or other projectile` AT MOST 5.7
            AND `the velocity in metres per second that a projectile it is designed or adapted to discharge is designed or adapted to attain` AT MOST 152.4
            AND `the energy in joules that a projectile it is designed or adapted to discharge is designed or adapted to attain` AT MOST 5.7

-- src:1991 | Exception — antique firearms
-- src:1992 | (3.1) Notwithstanding subsection (3), an antique firearm is a firearm for the purposes of regulations made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act and subsection 86(2) of this Act.
@ref s 84(3.1) (src:1991-1992)
GIVEN `s 84(1) antique firearm: the thing is an antique firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is regulations made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(3.1) the antique firearm is a firearm for the purpose` MEANS
    IF     `s 84(1) antique firearm: the thing is an antique firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (   `the purpose is regulations made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act`
            OR (provision's `section` EQUALS 86 AND provision's `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an antique firearm is a firearm for the purposes of regulations made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act and subsection 86(2) of this Act"

§ `Section 84(4) -- Meaning of holder`

-- src:1993 | Meaning of holder
-- src:1994 | (4) For the purposes of this Part, a person is the holder of
-- src:1995 | (a) an authorization or a licence if the authorization or licence has been issued to the person and the person continues to hold it; and
@ref s 84(4)(a) (src:1993-1995)
GIVEN `the authorization or licence has been issued to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person continues to hold it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(4)(a) the person is the holder of an authorization or a licence` MEANS
    IF     `the authorization or licence has been issued to the person`
       AND `the person continues to hold it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the authorization or licence has been issued to the person and the person continues to hold it" (marginal reading (a): a failed "if")

-- src:1996 | (b) a registration certificate for a firearm if
-- src:1997 | (i) the registration certificate has been issued to the person and the person continues to hold it, or
-- src:1998 | (ii) the person possesses the registration certificate with the permission of its lawful holder.
@ref s 84(4)(b) (src:1996-1998)
GIVEN `the registration certificate has been issued to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person continues to hold the registration certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses the registration certificate with the permission of its lawful holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(4)(b) the person is the holder of a registration certificate for a firearm` MEANS
    IF     (`the registration certificate has been issued to the person` AND `the person continues to hold the registration certificate`)
        OR `the person possesses the registration certificate with the permission of its lawful holder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a registration certificate for a firearm if" (marginal reading (a): a failed "if")

§ `Section 84(5) and (6) -- Subsequent offences`

-- src:1999 | Subsequent offences
-- src:2000 | (5) In determining, for the purpose of subsection 99(2), 100(2) or 103(2), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:2001 | (a) an offence under section 85, 95, 96, 98, 98.1, 99, 100, 102 or 103 or subsection 117.01(1);
-- src:2002 | (b) an offence under section 244 or 244.2; or
-- src:2003 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:2004 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref s 84(5) (src:1999-2004)
GIVEN `the subsection for which the question is asked` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the person spent in custody between those two days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(5) the earlier offence is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the subsection is one of those named`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of subsection 99(2), 100(2) or 103(2)"
        IF NOT (`the earlier offence is listed`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences" (marginal reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF `ten years have elapsed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the subsection is one of those named` MEANS
            (`the subsection for which the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 99 OR `the subsection for which the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 100 OR `the subsection for which the question is asked`'s `section` EQUALS 103)
            AND `the subsection for which the question is asked`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"
        -- (a) an offence under section 85, 95, 96, 98, 98.1, 99, 100, 102 or 103 or subsection 117.01(1)
        `limb (a)` MEANS
               `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 85
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 95
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 96
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 98
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 98.1
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 99
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 100
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 102
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 103
            OR (`the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 117.01 AND `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
        -- (b) an offence under section 244 or 244.2
        `limb (b)` MEANS
               `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 244
            OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 244.2
        -- (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence
        `limb (c)` MEANS
                (   `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 220
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 236
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 239
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 272
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 273
                 OR (`the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 279 AND `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 279.1
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 344
                 OR `the offence of which the person was earlier convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 346)
            AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`
        `the earlier offence is listed` MEANS `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)`
        -- However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
        -- Read: ten years after the earlier conviction, plus the days in custody, is on or before the later conviction (fork F-ten-years: on the tenth anniversary itself, ten years have elapsed).
        `ten years have elapsed` MEANS
            `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` AT LEAST ((`add years` `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` 10) PLUS `the number of days the person spent in custody between those two days`)

-- src:2005 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:2006 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref s 84(6) (src:2005-2006)
DECLARE `s 84(6) offence` HAS
    `the day on which it was committed`                       IS A DATE
    `the day on which the person was convicted of it`         IS A DATE

@ref s 84(6) (src:2005-2006)
GIVEN `offence one` IS A `s 84(6) offence`
      `offence two` IS A `s 84(6) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84(6) offence one is the earlier offence for the purposes of subsection (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `offence one`'s `the day on which the person was convicted of it` LESS THAN `offence two`'s `the day on which the person was convicted of it` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `offence one`'s `the day on which the person was convicted of it` GREATER THAN `offence two`'s `the day on which the person was convicted of it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how two convictions on the same day are sequenced
